16	10	Manifest: Rust MCP Tool Pattern	# Manifest: Rust MCP Tool Pattern (Macro-First)\n**Status:** Approved Coding Standard\n**Version:** 1.0.0\n**Date:** 2026-04-08\n\n## 1. The #[mcp_tool] Mandate\nTo ensure architectural consistency and prevent schema-sync bugs, all VibeMCP tools must use the `rust-mcp-sdk` procedural macro.\n\n### The Transformation Loop:\n1.  **Input:** Doc comments + Struct fields.\n2.  **Output:** Automatic JSON Schema generation (via `schemars`).\n3.  **Result:** The LLM always sees the exact parameters the code expects.\n\n## 2. Standard Implementation Pattern\nEvery tool must follow the **Context-Injected Implementation** pattern to ensure testability and fault isolation.\n\n```rust\n// 1. Tool Definition (Macro handles protocol glue)\n#[macros::mcp_tool(\n    name = "commit_artifact",\n    description = "Saves specification/plan to the Knowledge Hub"\n)]\n#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize, JsonSchema)]\npub struct CommitArtifact {\n    pub task_id: String,\n    pub content: String,\n}\n\n// 2. Business Logic (Pure and Testable)\nimpl CommitArtifact {\n    pub async fn execute_with_context(\n        &self,\n        ctx: &ToolContext,\n    ) -> Result<CallToolResult, CallToolError> {\n        // MANDATE: Always check Column Gating first\n        let task = ctx.api.get_task(&self.task_id).await?;\n        if task.column.name != "Specify" {\n             return Err(CallToolError::invalid_params("Not in Specify column"));\n        }\n\n        // Logic here...\n        Ok(CallToolResult::success("Artifact saved"))\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## 3. The "Two-Step" Governance Pattern\nFor actions that modify project rules (e.g., Constitution), the **Propose -> Confirm** pattern must be used.\n\n*   **Step 1:** `propose_X` returns a diff and a transient 16-char confirmation code.\n*   **Step 2:** `confirm_X` requires the code to be echoed back by the human.\n*   **State:** Codes are stored in an in-memory `Mutex<HashMap>` with a strict 5-minute TTL.\n\n## 4. Fault Isolation & Logging\n*   **No unwrap():** Use `?` or `ok_or_else()` to convert errors into `OrchestratorError`.\n*   **Standardized Headers:** Every tool that modifies code must trigger a comment starting with `📁 [FILES TOUCHED]`.\n*   **Internal Monologue:** Use the `internal_monologue` field for verbose Shrimp-style audits; keep comments concise.\n\n## 5. Defense-in-Depth Checklist\nBefore a tool implementation is considered "Ratified," it must pass:\n- [ ] **Column Affinity:** Does it verify the task column?\n- [ ] **Token Awareness:** Does it use the `ContextAssembler` budget?\n- [ ] **Error Mapping:** Does it map to `RpcError` without panicking?\n- [ ] **Statelessness:** Does it rely ONLY on the Hub API for data?\n	CONSTITUTION	1	1	2026-04-09 15:29:59.586	2026-04-09 15:29:59.586
17	10	Implementation: ContextAssembler Token Budgeting	## Core Token Budgeting Strategy\n\n### Budget Allocation\n- Metadata: 500 tokens\n- Persona (Column): 1000 tokens\n- Constitution: 1500 tokens (STRICT: Never summarized)\n- Specification: 2000 tokens (Adaptive: Summarized if needed)\n- Hard Limit: 5500 tokens (Effective context window)\n\n### Implementation Patterns\n- **Strict Mode:** Fail if budget exceeded.\n- **Adaptive Mode:** Use LLM to summarize SPECIFICATION while preserving MUST/SHALL requirements.\n- **Emergency Mode:** Aggressive truncation with visual warnings.\n\n### Logic Flow\n1. Fetch Task + Columns + Docs via `?inline=true`.\n2. Count tokens using `tiktoken-rs`.\n3. Verify Constitution fidelity.\n4. Apply summarization/truncation to Spec and Metadata.\n5. Assemble final prompt string.	SPECIFICATION	1	1	2026-04-09 15:42:02.319	2026-04-09 15:42:02.319
14	10	VibeMCP: Architectural Design [RATIFIED]	# Manifest: The Vibe Product Platform\n**Version:** 1.5.0 (Simple & Sovereign)\n**Status:** Architecture Ratified\n**Date:** 2026-04-09\n\n## 1. Core Vision: The Lattice\nVibe Tasks is a **Lifecycle-Driven Product Platform**. It provides a structured state machine (The Lattice) where Humans and Agents collaborate via a shared "Working Memory."\n\n### Architectural Philosophy (Finalized)\n*   **Simple is Beautiful:** One Delegate Key per MCP integration. No complex "Wallet" logic required in the binary.\n*   **Persona Sovereignty:** Agent identity is stateless and driven purely by the **Column Description** of the current task.\n*   **Protocol-First:** The Rust binary is a sidecar that enforces the Lattice Protocol via the verified `/api/agent` prefix.\n\n## 2. The Agent Protocol\n\n| Endpoint | Feature | Agent Benefit |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `GET .../me` | **Identity** | Binary confirms its assigned name and role metadata. |\n| `GET .../tasks/:id?inline=true` | **Context Packet** | Single-call JIT context (Metadata + Column Persona + Linked Docs). |\n| `POST .../tasks/:id/accept` | **Claim Logic** | Agent signals it has taken ownership of a ticket. |\n\n## 3. The "Intelligent Sidecar" (Rust MCP)\nThe Rust binary acts as the **Context Assembler** and **Security Enforcer**.\n\n### Key Responsibilities:\n1.  **Token Budgeting:** Strictly enforces 4k-5k token limits per task turn.\n2.  **Persona Injection:** Transforms Column Descriptions into high-fidelity System Prompts.\n3.  **Governance Gate:** Blocks destructive actions or Constitution modifications.\n\n---\n*Ratified for final implementation.*\n	SPECIFICATION	4	1	2026-04-09 14:42:29.808	2026-04-14 02:56:26.686
19	10	Feature Request: Admin Platform-Agent Bento Card	# Feature Request: Platform Agent Registry (Admin Hub)\n\n**Target UI:** `/dashboard/settings/admin` (Administration Bento Grid)  \n**Status:** Design Finalized  \n**Priority:** High\n\n## 1. Objective\nAdd a new administrative card to the Settings Hub specifically for managing **Platform-Level Agents**. Unlike project-specific agents, Platform Agents are intended for "Orchestrator" tools that handle system-wide health and project discovery.\n\n## 2. Requirement\nThe card should mirror the functionality of the **Agent Registry** found in Project Settings but target the system-wide scope.\n\n### UI Components:\n*   **Card Title:** "Platform Agent Registry"\n*   **Actions:**\n    *   `Rename`, `Enable/Disable`.\n    *   `Regenerate Key` (Rotates the system-wide key).\n    *   `Delete`.\n*   **Status Badges:** `Active`, `Expires`.\n\n## 3. Integration Path\n*   Use the existing **Create Agent** flow but route the request to a new admin-only endpoint: `POST /api/admin/platform-agents`.\n*   The resulting key should be tagged in `metadata` as `isPlatformAgent: true`.\n\n## 4. Permissions\n*   By default, Platform Agent keys should have **Zero project access**. \n*   They are restricted to non-destructive system calls: `GET /health`, `GET /api/agent/me`, and `GET /api/agent/projects/summary`.\n	SPECIFICATION	1	1	2026-04-09 17:22:33.718	2026-04-09 17:22:33.718
20	10	VibeMCP: Internal Business Logic Manual	# Specification: Business Logic Blueprint (Internal Algorithms)\n**Status:** Approved / Tier-Aware Logic\n**Version:** 1.3.0\n**Date:** 2026-04-10\n\n## 1. The Startup Identity Handshake\nThe binary MUST NOT assume its capabilities. It must perform a **Pre-flight Identity Check**.\n\n### Logic:\n1.  **Load Key:** Fetch active key from `--config vibe-mcp.toml`.\n2.  **Call /me:** Execute `GET /api/agent/me`.\n3.  **Tier Detection:**\n    *   IF `agent.metadata.isPlatformAgent == true`:\n        *   Set state to `PLATFORM_MODE`.\n        *   Filter available tools to: `query_projects`, `get_lattice_context`, `read_docs`.\n        *   Block all mutation tools at the protocol level.\n    *   IF `agent.metadata.isPlatformAgent == false`:\n        *   Set state to `PROJECT_MODE`.\n        *   Register full SpecKit/Shrimp toolset.\n        *   Cache `delegations` array for project-scoped permission checks.\n\n## 2. Dynamic Registry Management (The add_agent Tool)\nTo allow users to add identities via chat without manually editing TOML files.\n\n### The Registration Algorithm:\n1.  **Tool Invoke:** `register_agent(key: String)`.\n2.  **Verify:** Call `/api/agent/me` using the *provided* key.\n3.  **Inspect:** Parse the response for agent name and tier.\n4.  **Persist:** Append the validated identity to `agents` array in `vibe-mcp.toml`.\n5.  **Hash Policy:** Keys MUST NOT be stored in plain text if the environment is shared. Use OS-level secret storage or SHA-256 masking for logs.\n\n## 3. Pre-flight Access Gating (Client-Side)\nThe `VibeTaskClient` MUST implement a `check_access(method, path)` method.\n\n*   **Platform Guard:** IF `state == PLATFORM_MODE` and `method != GET`, return `ApiError::Forbidden`.\n*   **Whitelist Guard:** IF `state == PLATFORM_MODE`, verify `path` matches regex patterns in `configuredReadEndpoints`.\n*   **Project Guard:** IF `state == PROJECT_MODE`, verify `projectId` in path exists in the agent's `delegations` array.\n\n## 4. Context Synthesis (One-Call Packet)\nThe logic for `get_task_context` remains the "Zero Token" source of truth:\n1.  **Instruction Chaining:** Identity Header + Worktree Instruction + Constitution.\n2.  **Annotation Injection:** Harvest `#note` comments from history.\n3.  **Token Budgeting:** Strictly enforce 4000-token limit using adaptive summarization.\n	SPECIFICATION	3	1	2026-04-10 15:38:52.609	2026-04-10 16:06:23.804
21	10	Vision: Mission-Driven Lattice	# Vision: Mission-Driven Lattice (Modular Workflows)\n**Status:** Research Prototype / Post-MVP Vision\n**Date:** 2026-04-10\n**Inspiration:** Spec Kitty "Doctrine" System\n\n## 1. Objective\nTo transition Vibe Tasks from a "Software Development Kanban" into a **Universal Knowledge Work Engine**. By decoupling the state machine from the code and moving it into a "Mission YAML," the platform can support any structured workflow without backend changes.\n\n## 2. The Mission YAML Schema\nEvery project will link to a `mission.yaml` (stored in the Hub) that defines the project's "DNA."\n\n### Key Sections:\n*   **`states`**: Defines the column names and display order (e.g., `Scoping -> Gathering -> Synthesis`).\n*   **`guards`**: Algorithmic rules for moving between columns (e.g., `check: 'artifact_exists("SPECIFICATION.md")'`).\n*   **`artifacts`**: Required vs. Optional documents the agent must produce for each phase.\n*   **`mcp_tools`**: Whitelist of recommended tools for the domain (e.g., `arxiv-search` for Research, `seo-audit` for Marketing).\n*   **`agent_context`**: The "Base Persona" instructions injected as the top-level system prompt for the entire project.\n\n## 3. Dynamic Lattice Scaffolding\nWhen a new project is initialized via `/vibe.init --mission [type]`, the Rust binary will:\n1.  **Parse** the mission YAML.\n2.  **Bulk-create** the columns exactly as defined in the `states` array.\n3.  **Inject** the state-specific persona prompts into each `Column.description`.\n\n## 4. Mission-Aware Tool Filtering\nThe Rust MCP server will dynamically register tools based on the mission's `mcp_tools` section.\n*   **Goal:** Protect the LLM from "Tool Overload." \n*   **Result:** A Research Agent only sees tools for reading PDFs and searching citations, while a Software Agent sees tools for tests and code indexing.\n\n## 5. Implementation Roadmap (Phase 4)\n*   [ ] Create `vibe-missions` Hub repository.\n*   [ ] Implement YAML expression evaluator in the Rust binary (`guards` engine).\n*   [ ] Add "Mission Selector" to the Vibe UI Project Creation flow.\n	BRAINSTORM	1	1	2026-04-10 16:41:12.169	2026-04-10 16:41:12.169
22	10	Vision: OpenFang Swarm Integration	# Vision: OpenFang Swarm Integration\n**Status:** Architecture Finalized / Ready for Plugin Implementation\n**Version:** 1.0.0\n**Date:** 2026-04-10\n\n## 1. Objective\nTo leverage **OpenFang** as the primary runtime environment (The Laborer Swarm) for Vibe Tasks. OpenFang provides the process management, security sandboxing, and channel adapters (IRC/Discord) needed to transform VibeMCP tools into autonomous behaviors.\n\n## 2. Integration Architecture (The "Bolt-On" Model)\n\n### A. VibeMCP as a Provider\nThe `vibe-mcp-binary` is registered as an external server in `openfang.toml`. \n*   OpenFang agents gain namespaced tools: `mcp_vibe_get_task_context`, `mcp_vibe_commit_spec`, etc.\n*   This allows any OpenFang agent (regardless of its internal model) to interact with the Kanban Lattice.\n\n### B. Event-Driven Invocation (The Bridge)\nA small background process (Vibe-Relay) monitors the VibeTask WebSocket feed.\n1.  **Event:** Task #58 moved to `Verify`.\n2.  **Relay:** Vibe-Relay emits a `SystemEvent` to the OpenFang Kernel.\n3.  **Trigger:** OpenFang's `TriggerEngine` identifies a match for the "Critic" persona.\n4.  **Wake-up:** The `CriticBot` is spawned/activated with the task context as its initial prompt.\n\n### C. The IRC War Room (Observability)\nOpenFang’s IRC channel adapter is used to provide a human-readable "Lobby" for the swarm.\n*   **Machine Traffic:** High-speed data (NATS) remains internal to OpenFang.\n*   **Reasoning Traffic:** Bots discuss architectural decisions in the `#vibe-swarm` IRC channel.\n*   **Human Oversight:** The user can monitor the discussion via an IRC-compatible TUI (Vibe-Overwatch).\n\n## 3. Decision Compaction (Zero-Token Efficiency)\n*   Agents use IRC for "Chatter" and "Argumentation."\n*   Once a consensus is reached, the lead agent uses the `mcp_vibe_commit_artifact` tool to save the **Final Technical Decision** to the VibeTask Knowledge Hub.\n*   This ensures the Cloud Bot (Cursor/Claude) only sees the high-fidelity results, not the messy discussion.\n\n## 4. Resource Allocation\nWe use OpenFang's **`openfang-runtime`** to manage local resources:\n*   **ResearchBot:** Assigned high CPU/Memory for code indexing.\n*   **CriticBot:** Assigned low resources for lightweight verification.\n*   **WorkerBot:** Isolated in a `subprocess_sandbox` for safe code execution.\n	BRAINSTORM	1	1	2026-04-10 18:44:54.994	2026-04-10 18:44:54.994
23	10	[RESOLVED] Bug Report: Missing Agent API Endpoints	# Bug Report: Missing Agent-Scoped API Endpoints (404 Not Found)\n\n**Severity:** High (Blocks Agent Workflow)\n**Component:** Backend (`src/api/routes/agent/*`)\n**Date:** 2026-04-10\n\n## 1. Summary\nDuring stress testing of the "Agent-Lean" protocol on Project 10, several critical endpoints returned `404 Not Found`. While the `unifiedAuthMiddleware` is functioning correctly, the corresponding sub-routers for Documents and Doc-Links have not been registered within the `agentRouter`, and the Project Summary aggregator is missing from the projects sub-router.\n\n## 2. Evidence of Gaps\n\n### A. Missing Project Summary Aggregator\n*   **Endpoint:** `GET /api/agent/projects/summary`\n*   **Behavior:** Returns 404.\n*   **Implementation Note:** This endpoint is required for the "Push-back" protocol to allow agents to list project formality levels and metadata without fetching full task lists.\n\n### B. Missing Knowledge Hub (Documents)\n*   **Endpoint:** `GET /api/agent/projects/:projectId/docs`\n*   **Endpoint:** `POST /api/agent/projects/:projectId/docs`\n*   **Behavior:** Returns 404.\n*   **Observation:** The standard `documentsRoutes` are mounted at the root level using `requireAuth`. They need to be exposed under the `/api/agent` prefix using `unifiedAuthMiddleware` and `requireAgentProjectAccess`.\n\n### C. Missing Context Binding (Doc-Links)\n*   **Endpoint:** `POST /api/agent/projects/:projectId/tasks/:taskId/doc-links`\n*   **Behavior:** Returns 404.\n*   **Observation:** Like the documents routes, these are currently restricted to human-only authentication.\n\n## 3. Implementation Checklist for Dev Team\n\n### Permissions Layer (`src/infrastructure/auth/agent-permissions.ts`)\n*   [ ] Add `VIEW_DOCS = 'docs:view'` to `ProjectAction`.\n*   [ ] Add `CREATE_DOC = 'docs:create'` to `ProjectAction`.\n*   [ ] Map both actions in `ACTION_PERMISSIONS` (VIEW_DOCS -> VIEWER, CREATE_DOC -> USER).\n\n### Project Router (`src/api/routes/agent/projects.ts`)\n*   [ ] Implement `GET /summary` to return an array of `{ id, name, formalityLevel, totalTasks, activeSprints }`.\n\n### Agent Router Index (`src/api/routes/agent/index.ts`)\n*   [ ] Register the new `documentsRouter` at `/projects/:projectId/docs`.\n*   [ ] Register the new `docLinksRouter` at `/projects/:projectId/tasks/:taskId/doc-links`.\n\n## 4. Note on Database State\nA desync was discovered where **Project 10** had 0 members, causing `403 Forbidden` for all entities. This was manually patched via `psql` (User 1 restored as Owner), but the backend team should verify why project creation/member-creation transactions might be failing during recent refactors.\n	SPECIFICATION	2	1	2026-04-11 10:52:12.987	2026-04-12 00:11:56.717
